This differs from a throttle function, which limits the execution of a function to a certain number of times within a given time period. While debounce ensures that functions are not executed too quickly, throttle ensures that they are not executed at all during that time period.

A debounce function is a mechanism that prevents multiple actions from occurring immediately after each other when the event rate exceeds a certain threshold. It achieves this by introducing a delay between consecutive events, allowing only the most recent action to be processed.

