## Debounce vs Throttle

| Aspect | Debounce | Throttle |
|--------|----------|----------|
| **Execution** | Runs once after waiting stops | Runs periodically while active |
| **Use case** | Search input, resize handlers | Scroll events, mousemove |
| **Behavior** | Waits for a pause in activity | Limits execution frequency |

**Example**: Type "hello" with 100ms debounce—search runs once after you stop typing. With throttle at 500ms intervals—search runs multiple times while typing continues.

Debounce suits one-time actions; throttle suits continuous monitoring.

